<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Güyük Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1206">1206</a>–<a href="/years/1248">1248</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Güyük Khan was the third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, reigning from 1246 to 1248. A son of Ögedei, he campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> in 1233, when his army captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puxian-wannu">Puxian Wannu</a> of Eastern Xia, and later took part in the western campaign against the Rus'. He was elected after a long regency by his mother Töregene and died while marching west, apparently to confront his cousin Batu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guyuk-khan.jpg" alt="Güyük Khan" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abdullâh Sultân (atelier). Shîrâz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guyuk_khan_from_Persian_miniature.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
